cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Monteverde, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Monteverde: ClayPVersusNP is equivalent to CslibPEqNP, in Lean 4"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 proof that ClayPVersusNP, the LeanMillenniumPrizeProblems formalization of
  Cook's P vs NP statement, is equivalent to P = NP for every encoding in cslib-frontier.
  The proof uses only the axioms propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. The equivalence
  is at the level of statements; it does not decide either side. Developed with AI
  assistance (Claude, by Anthropic); every proof is checked by the Lean kernel and,
  independently, by nanoda.
